 president obama's tweet that he  sent in the in the wake of this uh  decision from the jury  are you still in touch with with the  president do you still advise him  so yeah we are honored to stay close to  the both the former president and the  obama foundation and support wherever we  can yeah  have you talked to him about this not  about this subject no yeah  i'm wondering what you would uh you know  give me an idea of what you have been  been speaking with him about and  and give us an idea of what he's been  thinking about since he has left office  and we've seen the conversation about  race change so much  well you know what i've seen the former  president and the former first lady  focus on is long-term systemic change so  for example with their my brother's  keeper initiative  thinking about how they can pour into  men and boys of color in the long run  setting up mentoring programs and  and other initiatives to really  strengthen those communities or the  first lady's efforts with women and  girls you know this is a  again a long journey we've been on as a  country we've  you know from slavery to jim crow to the  civil rights era and now we've had  basically  350 years of really tough stuff in just  50 or 60 years where we're just  beginning  to figure some of these pieces out and  so what i've always appreciated about  the former president and and first lady  is that they're focused on the long run  and that's where their interventions  have been  and joshua i mean we're still seeing  corporations that are  are sometimes making these mistakes  right and making these embarrassing gaps  as you've noted uh what are three things  that you would advise them  if you were talking to them today well  first thing is  assess the tools that they're using to  evaluate you know their messaging  and and their ad campaigns and making  sure that those tools are inclusive  the second thing is listen to their  diverse employees right they're folks  that are  within these o